{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:35e7424b620cd2d7eebfa1730fded974", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 9, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "I already applied this edit in my previous turn - `config.json` now has `\"/\"` set to `cache_control: \"no-store\"` and `\"/static/\"` set to `cache_control: \"public, max-age=31536000\"`. There's no further pending edit to make; the file currently reads:\n\n```json\n{\n\"listen\": 8080,\n\"routes\": [\n{\n\"path\": \"/\",\n\"upstream\": \"app:3000\",\n\"cache_control\": \"no-store\"\n},\n{\n\"path\": \"/static/\",\n\"upstream\": \"assets:9000\",\n\"cache_control\": \"public, max-age=31536000\"\n}\n]\n}\n```\n\nAs noted before, this is a chosen resolution of a genuine conflict between the two review comments, not a literal simultaneous satisfaction of both (which isn't possible with one `cache_control` value per route). If that tradeoff isn't the one you want, let me know which comment should take precedence for `/static/` and I'll adjust.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:fe3a33afc99e6832b83b10d2973ac832"}
